      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T07:01:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the input. Below is our answers for your concern:\n\n1. No, and we are highly aware of that kind of information is sensitive.\nWe\u0027ll redact it before publishing to anyone else. See aosp/1542746.\nJust like what we did for SSID and other sensitive information in NetworkCapabilities.\nThe one who is going to use this is for NetworkStatsService to index the data usage. We want to use subId if we could, but currently there are 2 concerns of it:\n  a. subId changes per SDK update, this cannot be used for NetworkStats.\n  b. From what we learned, subId \u0026 subscriberId is not strictly 1-1 mapping. We already have subId in the NetworkSpecifier inside NetworkCapabilities but in short/mid term we cannot use that.\n\n2. After internal discussion, we\u0027ll reject any update of IMSI inside ConnectivityService once it has been set, then it could act like what\nwe did in NetworkAgentConfig.\n\n3. Today the information is already passed by networkAgentConfig so there is no behavior change for that. ConnectivityService/NetworkStatsSerivce/NetworkPolicyManagerService can already deal with null/empty IMSI string.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "f5d27465_520ec081",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1659,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 1659,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "ae4e8b2951818dc7242a8534eb14a61ddbf74812",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1593fed9_e8db0543",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DataConnection.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1659,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T23:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "subId does not change after SDK update, and it is 1:1 mapping to subscriber id in our implementation (i.e. TelephonyManager.getSubscriberId() only returns one IMSI). We don\u0027t support two subscriptions in one SIM today (and it does not exist in real world either).\n\nAnother concern is that they will be gated by different permissions now. One is android.Manifest.permission.NETWORK_SETTINGS and the other one is android.Manifest.permission.READ_PRIVILEGED_PHONE_STATE (and their protection level is different). Even though they are the same protection level, gating the information by different permissions is not a good practice and can lead trouble in the future if someone just mistakenly change its protection level for other purposes.\n\nI spent some time before to eliminate IMSI as being used as index outside of telephony (i.e. NetworkStatsService) before but just didn\u0027t have time to finish it. I was doing that because 1. IMSI is a sensitive PII info, 2. sub id is created for that purposes.\n\nWill you have a long term plan migrating to use sub id in NetworkStatsService? If yes, I am okay with this as a short term solution.",
      "parentUuid": "8cf4e176_236bb74c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1659,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 1659,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "ae4e8b2951818dc7242a8534eb14a61ddbf74812",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
